rescue teams in china are still  searching for possible survivors from a  crashed passenger jet so far no one has  been found alive the china eastern  airlines plane came down in the  mountains near wu zhu in the south of  the country on monday there were 123  passengers and nine crew on board  witnesses have described seeing the  plane fall in a near vertical descent  it is hoped that the flight recorders  will be found and provide key answers as  to why the plane crashed china has one  of the best airline safety records in  the world  rescuers scour the mountains of guanxi  for signs of life  the boeing 737 scattered across a remote  forest after falling from the sky  villagers nearby described the moment  the plane went down  [Music]  i heard a loud  people were doing their work peeling  tree bark  but they stopped everything  and rushed to see the crash  then the police arrived  shows the plane plunged 26 000 feet in  just three minutes  it's the country's first commercial air  crash since 2010.  china eastern airlines has grounded all  boeing 737-800 planes in its fleet  china's president expressed his shock an  immediate investigation has been ordered  we are deeply saddened by the accident  of the china eastern airlines passenger  flight  every effort to organize search and  rescue is being made  and we will find out the cause of the  accident as soon as possible to ensure  the absolute safety of aviation  operations  at guangzhou airport the plane's  destination families wait for news from  the mountainside  the flight data recorders could provide  clues as to what brought the plane down  but such investigations can take months  or even years
 

